\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Boeing\uc2  Says It Has Made Its 'Best and Final' Offer to Workers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Niraj Chokshi \par \uc2 590 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The proposal includes raises of 30 percent over the four-year contract, up from a 25 percent offer, but it's unclear whether it will satisfy workers.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  on Monday made what it described as its ''best and final'' contract offer to more than 33,000 striking union employees.\par \par \uc2 The proposal offers benefits beyond those in a tentative contract that the employees, who are represented by the \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers\uc2 , resoundingly rejected less than two weeks earlier. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  gave the workers, most of whom work in commercial aircraft production in the Seattle area, until the end of Friday to accept the offer.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and the union restarted negotiations last week with the help of a federal mediator. The talks ended on Wednesday with no further negotiation dates scheduled, the union said at the time.\par \par \uc2 Brian Bryant, the international president of the union, said in a statement on Monday that the organization was reviewing the offer.\par \par \uc2 ''Employees knew \uc2 Boeing\uc2  executives could do better, and this shows the workers were right all along,'' he said. ''The proposal will be analyzed to see if it's up to the task of helping workers gain adequate ground on prior sacrifices.''\par \par \uc2 The new proposal includes raises of 30 percent over the four-year term of the contract, up from the previous 25 percent offer. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  said it would give each worker $6,000 for approving the deal, double a previous offer. It would also reinstate performance bonuses that were set to be cut and increase a company match for employee 401(k) contributions. The rest is the same as the previous offer.\par \par \uc2 It isn't clear whether the offer will satisfy the demands of workers, who were widely frustrated over raises, retirement benefits and other parts of the previous proposal. That deal was rejected by more than 95 percent of the union members who voted on it on Sept. 12, although union leaders had recommended approval. A slightly larger share voted to walk out.\par \par \uc2 The strike has virtually halted \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's commercial aircraft production. The company makes the 737 Max, its most popular jet, and other planes in the Seattle region, though it also makes the 787 Dreamliner at a nonunion factory in South Carolina. The company had already fallen behind on deliveries of the Max because federal regulators capped production after a panel blew out of one of the planes during a flight in January.\par \par \uc2 That incident set off a crisis of confidence at \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , forcing it to make several changes aimed at improving quality and safety. It also led to a management shake-up, which culminated in the appointment of a new chief executive, \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2 , last month.\par \par \uc2 The strike cost the company at least $571 million in its first week, according to an estimate by Anderson Economic Group, a research and consulting firm in Michigan. Within days of the walkout, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  enacted a series of cost-cutting measures, including furloughs of white-collar employees.\par \par \uc2 Leaders of a different union, the \uc2 Society of Professional Engineering Employees in Aerospace\uc2 , rejected the furloughs, saying its contract with \uc2 Boeing\uc2  prohibited the company from imposing them on its members, which include engineers and technical workers.\par \par \uc2 ''We don't see any compelling reason to change the provisions of our collective bargaining agreement,'' John Dimas, the union's president, said in a statement last week. ''We rejected the request.''\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page B3. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240924ek9o0003x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
