\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 F.B.I. Boards Ship Linked To Collapse\b0\par\par\uc2 By Amy Qin \par \uc2 446 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 September 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 15\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The move comes three days after the Justice Department's civil lawsuit against the owner and operator of the Dali, which struck the Francis Scott Key Bridge in March.\par \par \uc2 F.B.I. agents on Saturday boarded a container ship that is managed by the same parent company as the cargo vessel that collided with the Francis Scott Key Bridge in Baltimore in March, which had toppled the structure and killed six workers.\par \par \uc2 The agents were conducting ''court-authorized law enforcement activity'' on the Maersk Saltoro ship alongside officials from the Coast Guard's Investigative Service and the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 's Criminal Investigation division, according to statements from the F.B.I. and the U.S. attorney's office in Maryland.\par \par \uc2 Both the Maersk Saltoro, currently also in Baltimore, and the Dali, the container ship that crashed in March, are managed by Synergy Marine Group, which is based in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 The activity, which was first reported by \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2 , comes just three days after the \uc2 U.S. Justice Department\uc2  filed a lawsuit against the owner and operator of the Dali for being ''grossly negligent'' and ''reckless'' in the lead-up to the collision.\par \par \uc2 The government is seeking more than $100 million in damages to cover the costs of the sprawling emergency response to the disaster and the federal aid to port employees who were put out of work. The Dali is owned by Grace Ocean Ltd., also based in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Officials did not provide more details on Saturday's boarding and did not say if it was connected to the Justice Department's lawsuit or a separate federal criminal investigation into the crash that remains active.\par \par \uc2 The Maersk Saltoro was sailing under the Singaporean flag and was expected to depart for Sri Lanka, according to VesselFinder, a ship tracking website. Grace Ocean did not immediately respond to a request for comment on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department lawsuit, which was filed in federal court on Wednesday in Maryland, described a series of failures onboard that resulted in the Dali losing power and slamming into the Key Bridge on March 26. The disaster could have been prevented at multiple points, the suit asserts, pointing to poor maintenance and ''jury-rigged'' fixes to serious problems aboard the ship.\par \par \uc2 The early-morning collapse of the bridge killed the six men who were repairing pavement on it and paralyzed the Port of Baltimore for weeks. On Tuesday, the families of three of the men who were killed announced that they were also suing the owner of the Dali.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A15. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240922ek9m0005i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
