\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters and The Associated Press \par \uc2 482 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 August 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 AUTOMOTIVE\par \par \uc2 G.M. Is Laying Off\par \par \uc2 Over 1,000 Employees\par \par \uc2 General Motors\uc2  said Monday it is laying off more than 1,000 salaried employees at its software and service units worldwide.\par \par \uc2 G.M., confirming the layoffs initially reported by CNBC, said that ''as we build G.M.'s future, we must simplify for speed and excellence, make bold choices, and prioritize the investments that will have the greatest impact.''\par \par \uc2 CNBC said the job cuts include roughly 600 jobs at G.M.'s tech campus near Detroit. G.M., which said about half of the cuts are in the United States, said the cuts were not because of cost cuts but came after a review of operations following the March departure of Mike Abbott, executive vice president of software and services who left because ofhealth reasons.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Abbott, a former Apple executive, was hired in 2023 to spearhead G.M.'s software development efforts amid an investment rampup from the automaker in electric vehicles and subscription-based services. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 LITIGATION\par \par \uc2 Triple Damages Sought\par \par \uc2 In Live Nation Lawsuit\par \par \uc2 Attorneys general from about two dozen U.S. states are seeking triple damages against \uc2 Live Nation Entertainment\uc2  and its ticket-selling unit, \uc2 Ticketmaster\uc2 , for allegedly monopolizing markets across the live concert industry in an updated version of a lawsuit originally filed in May.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Justice Department\uc2  and several states sued three months ago to break up Live Nation, arguing the concert promoter and \uc2 Ticketmaster\uc2  illegally inflated concert ticket prices and hurt artists.\par \par \uc2 Some states had sought damages under state law in the original lawsuit. By adding claims under the federal anti-monopoly law, states can seek three times the monetary damages.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, ten states joined the lawsuit filed in Manhattan federal court, and 26 states and the District of Columbia added claims for triple damages on behalf of their residents. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 CONSUMER SAFETY\par \par \uc2 Perdue Recalls Chicken After Metal Wire Found\par \par \uc2 Check your freezer. \uc2 Perdue Foods\uc2  is recalling more than 167,000 pounds of frozen chicken nuggets and tenders after some customers reported finding metal wire embedded in the products.\par \par \uc2 According to Perdue and the \uc2 U.S. Agriculture Department's Food Safety and Inspection Service\uc2 , the recall covers three products: Perdue Breaded Chicken Tenders, Butcher Box Organic Chicken Breast \uc2 Nuggets\uc2  and Perdue Simply Smart Organics Breaded Chicken Breast \uc2 Nuggets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The inspection service and \uc2 Perdue\uc2  determined that some 167,171 pounds of these products may be contaminated. \uc2 Perdue\uc2  said Friday that the material was ''identified in a limited number of consumer packages.''\par \par \uc2 The company later ''determined the material to be a very thin strand of metal wire,'' Jeff Shaw, \uc2 Perdue\uc2 's senior vice president of food safety and quality, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY NATHAN RAY SEEBECK/USA TODAY SPORTS VIA REUTERS) This article appeared in print on page B2. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240820ek8k0004u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
