\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Paramount\uc2  Will Lay Off 15% of Its U.S. Employees\b0\par\par\uc2 By Benjamin Mullin \par \uc2 572 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 August 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The company is cutting staff ahead of its merger next year with the Hollywood studio Skydance.\par \par \uc2 Paramount\uc2 , the parent company of CBS, Nickelodeon and \uc2 MTV\uc2 , told its employees on Tuesday it was beginning a series of long-scheduled job cuts that would winnow its staff by roughly 15 percent in the United States.\par \par \uc2 The company's three co-chief executives said in an internal note that the cuts -- which would be ''incredibly hard'' -- were necessitated by shifts in the entertainment industry.\par \par \uc2 ''The industry continues to evolve, and \uc2 Paramount\uc2  is at an inflection point where changes must be made to strengthen our business,'' said the note from \uc2 Brian Robbins\uc2 , the head of \uc2 Paramount Pictures\uc2 ; \uc2 George Cheeks\uc2 , the head of CBS; and \uc2 Chris McCarthy\uc2 , the head of \uc2 Showtime\uc2  and MTV Entertainment Studios.\par \par \uc2 The layoffs, which will affect thousands of employees, are the latest in a series of cutbacks by major media players. \uc2 Warner Bros. Discovery\uc2 , the parent of CNN, TNT and \uc2 HBO\uc2 , has slashed its staff routinely in recent years as it pays down billions in debt. \uc2 Disney\uc2  laid off more than 100 employees in its TV division last month.\par \par \uc2 The sweeping cuts at \uc2 Paramount\uc2  will affect many functions across the company, as it seeks to reduce its annual costs by roughly $500 million. They will largely be completed by the end of September, the chief executives said in their note.\par \par \uc2 In July, \uc2 Paramount\uc2  announced plans to merge with Skydance, the Hollywood studio that has co-produced hits like ''Top Gun: Maverick'' and ''Mission: Impossible -- Dead Reckoning Part One.'' Skydance's founder, the Hollywood producer \uc2 David Ellison\uc2 , is the son of \uc2 Larry Ellison\uc2 , founder of the software giant \uc2 Oracle\uc2 . The Ellison family is spending lavishly to finance a deal that includes $8 billion in capital.\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Paramount\uc2  readies for its merger with Skydance, it is also exploring other options. The company has a 45-day ''go shop'' window, allowing it to see if other suitors will top Skydance's bid. Among the interested parties is \uc2 Edgar Bronfman Jr.\uc2 , the former chief executive of \uc2 Warner Music Group\uc2 , who has been pursuing a bid for \uc2 Paramount\uc2  in recent days.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Paramount\uc2  reported earnings last week, executives told investors that its streaming business was profitable -- a relatively rare occurrence in the traditional media industry -- driven partly by the ad-supported streaming service Pluto TV. Paramount+, the company's flagship streaming service, lost 2.8 million subscribers last quarter, which the company attributed to an exit from a bundle agreement in South Korea.\par \par \uc2 The media industry has been through a series of mergers over the past decade that have mostly resulted in fewer jobs for people at the new conglomerates. The shrinking of the cable bundle, once the main growth engine for TV companies, has prompted executives to cut costs and team up with rivals to beef up their content libraries.\par \par \uc2 Those moves have done little for investors. The share prices of almost every traditional media company are down over the last five years, as investors remain skeptical that profits from streaming will replace those from cable.\par \par \uc2 Sweeping cuts will affect many functions at Paramount, the parent company of CBS, Nickelodeon and MTV, as it seeks to cut costs by $500 million a year. (PHOTOGRAPH BY MARK ABRAMSON FOR THE NEW YORK TIMES) This article appeared in print on page B4. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240814ek8e00049\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
