\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 World of Warcraft Staff At \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  Vote In Union\b0\par\par\uc2 By John Yoon \par \uc2 325 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 July 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The move adds more than 500 to the unionized video game staff at \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , which has pledged to remain neutral on organizing efforts.\par \par \uc2 More than 500 workers in the team behind World of Warcraft, one of the most popular video games in the world, have voted to unionize, the \uc2 Communications Workers of America\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The move expands the ranks of organized labor at \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , which acquired the video game giant \uc2 Activision Blizzard\uc2  -- whose subsidiary \uc2 Blizzard Entertainment\uc2  produces World of Warcraft -- for $69 billion last year. To satisfy the regulators overseeing the mega-acquisition, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  promised to remain neutral on unionizing efforts, an unusually permissive policy in the tech industry.\par \par \uc2 An arbitrator determined on Wednesday that a majority of the World of Warcraft workers, including designers, engineers, artists and quality testers, supported the C.W.A., the union said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Blizzard Entertainment\uc2  recognized the union, increasing the number of unionized game workers at \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  to more than 1,750, the C.W.A. said.\par \par \uc2 World of Warcraft, released in 2004, was a landmark game in the multiplayer role-playing genre. It allowed thousands of players to simultaneously explore a vast fantasy world, and generated billions of dollars in revenue for Blizzard.\par \par \uc2 Workers staged a walkout at \uc2 Blizzard Entertainment\uc2 's headquarters in 2021 after \uc2 California's Department of Fair Employment and Housing\uc2  accused \uc2 Activision Blizzard\uc2  of fostering a culture of sexual harassment and discrimination against female employees.\par \par \uc2 About 600 workers at \uc2 Activision Publishing\uc2 , another \uc2 Activision Blizzard\uc2  subsidiary, voted to unionize in March, forming the largest video game workers' union in the United States. Bethesda Game Studios also joined the C.W.A. last week, adding about 240 more game developers to the group of unionized workers at \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  recognized both unions.\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY JEFF GRITCHEN/THE ORANGE COUNTY REGISTER) This article appeared in print on page B4. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020240726ek7q0004r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
